# Exclude everything by default, then re-include only what the image needs.
*

# Re-include the build inputs the Dockerfile copies (Node server + static site).
!server/
!server/**
!site/
!site/**

# Never ship installed deps into the build context — the image runs `npm ci`.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# Belt-and-suspenders: explicitly drop internal/business docs and VCS/CI cruft.
# (These are already excluded by the `*` rule above, but listed for clarity so
# they can never accidentally land in the build context or image.)
CLAUDE.md
dugri_plan.html
resources/
.git/
.github/
.netlify/
*.md
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# The API also spawns the Python generator (previews + order PDFs), so the image
# needs the generator code AND the theme assets it reads at runtime. Re-include
# them AFTER the blanket excludes above so these rules win.
#
# Generator code, recipes, themes.json and the shared word-font pool.
!generator/
!generator/**
**/__pycache__/

# Each theme's WHOLE directory — clean/ + filled/ + fonts/ + assets/.
#
# filled/ used to be excluded right here, as "heavy Canva reference exports, not
# used at runtime". That stopped being true, and it cost the owner real files:
#
#  1. Since #253 the SERVER runs generator/recipe_diff.py at template upload and
#     diffs clean/ against filled/ to detect the card slots. With filled/ absent
#     from the image, detection could only ever work on files uploaded in that
#     same session — a shipped template could never be re-detected.
#  2. "שחזור למקור" deletes the owner's uploaded assets and falls back to the
#     shipped ones. With no shipped filled/ to fall back TO, a revert on
#     grapefruit wiped all nine filled/*.svg and both fonts, unrecoverably.
#
# Cost: ~65MB across the eight themes, and shrinking — a MIGRATED theme's filled/
# references ../assets/ instead of embedding rasters, so grapefruit is 704K
# against 15M for an unmigrated one. Including only the migrated themes would have
# left the other seven able to destroy the owner's uploads, which is not a trade
# worth ~60MB on an image that already carries Chromium.
!resources/
!resources/canva/
!resources/canva/templates/
!resources/canva/templates/**

# The press export (generator/press.py) converts an order to CMYK against this
# ICC profile, read off disk at request time. It lives under resources/, which
# the blanket rule above drops, so without this re-include the file is committed
# to git yet absent from the image and the admin button answers
#   500 press ICC profile missing  /app/resources/print shop/SWOP2006_Coated3v2.icc
# Only the profile: the folder's sample PDFs stay out of the build context.
!resources/print shop/
resources/print shop/*
!resources/print shop/SWOP2006_Coated3v2.icc

# The seed word pools (content/wordlists/*.txt) that generator/topup.py reads to
# top a short order up to a full deck. The `*` above excludes everything, so the
# Dockerfile's `COPY content/` needs these re-includes or the build has nothing to
# copy (that broke every order under a full deck — #216 added the COPY but not this).
!content/
!content/**
